<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duke Zhuang of Zheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 743–701 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duke Zhuang of Zheng (reigned 743–701 BCE) was a ruler of the State of Zheng who made it the leading state of the early Spring and Autumn period. He defeated a revolt by his younger brother Gongshu Duan and quarrelled with the Zhou court, where he had served as a minister. In 707 BCE his army defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-huan-of-zhou">King Huan of Zhou</a> at Xuge and wounded the king, a blow to royal prestige.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duke-zhuang-of-zheng.jpg" alt="Duke Zhuang of Zheng" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 馮夢龍 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E9%84%AD%E8%8E%8A%E5%85%AC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
